1. Scope and definitions

"Software" means the original code and documentation of this template, including
copies and adaptations that incorporate that material. Third-party components
remain subject to their respective licenses, as listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

"Personal Use" means using the Software for a natural person's own activities,
without commercializing the Software or services directly based on it.

"Internal Use" means use of the Software by a person or organization to
manage its own activities, agents, projects and information, without
offering it as a product or service to customers or other third parties. A
company's internal use is free of charge, even if the company is for-profit.

"Commercialization" means commercially exploiting the Software, or copies or
adaptations of it, through sale, resale, licensing, subscription, paid access,
offering as a hosted service, or integration into a commercial product for third
parties. It also includes charging third parties for deployment, customization,
operation, maintenance or support specifically related to this Software.

Revenue from one's own activities that merely use the Software as an internal
tool does not constitute Commercialization. Payment for generic infrastructure,
such as computing or storage used for one's own internal installation, does not
turn that use into Commercialization of the Software.

